# Raw Python Image Processing Engine #

A high-performance, command-line image editing tool built entirely from scratch in pure Python.
**No OpenCV. No NumPy. Just raw math, matrix manipulations, and heavily optimized algorithmic design**

This project was built to demonstrate a deep understanding of core computational photography algorithms and time/space complexity optimizations.

## Key Features & Algorithmic Optimizations
* **O(1) Adaptive Edge Detection:** Implements a Summed Area Table (Integral Image) algorithm,
dropping the time complexity of local-mean thresholding to exactly O(N) for the entire image, regardless of block size.
* **Lightning-Fast Pixel Mapping:** Uses pre-computed Look-Up Tables (LUTs) and C-optimized nested list comprehensions for O(1) quantization, grayscale conversion, and color manipulation.
* **Optimized Matrix Convolutions:** Implements "clamp-to-edge" image padding to entirely remove innermost bounds-checking during kernel matrix dot-products.
* **Sub-Pixel Geometry:** Features accurate Bilinear Interpolation for smooth, artifact-free image resizing.

## Supported Operations
1.  Grayscale Conversion
2.  Matrix Convolutions (Gaussian Blur, Sharpen, Emboss)
3.  Bilinear Interpolation Resizing
4.  Matrix Transposition (90° Rotations)
5.  Adaptive Thresholding (Edge Detection)
6.  LUT Quantization
7.  Sepia Filtering
8.  Color Inversion & Brightness Adjustment
9.  Geometric Flipping (Horizontal/Vertical)

## Installation & Usage
All you need is Python3.